From 806ce108d3cfe9b4000990ea5f476b1bf58fa3ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuk3s <44327449+nuk3s@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:28:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kv-offload): make the retry of an overrun load a cold
 prefill

Upstream base: the patch applies to local-inference-lab/vllm at
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 after the 702 patches of
spark-ds41f-1120 (candidate-62, 0001 to 0829) and patches 9030 to 9042
of this series.

Rationale: after an overrun the tier stays up and keeps the blocks, so
the retry of the same request found the same hit and started the same
load on the same slow path. While the path stayed slow, every attempt
overran at the same bound and the request never prefilled, and nothing
counted or bounded the attempts. With this patch the scheduler remembers
each request whose disk load overran and answers that request's later
lookups with a miss until the request finishes. The core scheduler
retries a failed load from 0 tokens, so the retry is now a cold
prefill, and the request does not overrun again before it finishes,
while other requests keep their hits and the tier stays up. The start
line of both bounds in the worker now ends with the rank, so each rank
logs its own line. A test of the slowest-load gauge also changes: the
gauge is rounded to 1 ms, and the two steps of that test can run within
0.5 ms, so the old check, which needed a reading above 0 ms, failed on a
fast machine.

Quality implications: the patch does not change outputs. A request
whose load overran pays one full prefill on its retry. Patch 9044
narrows the mark to the cold retry.

Tests: on the CPU path the offload suite passed 205 tests, with 2
CUDA-only modules skipped. Of the 4 new tests, the first checks that the
retry after an overrun gets 0 external tokens and pins nothing while a
new request with the same prompt still hits. The second runs five
overruns in a row, which end with every retry cold, five load failures,
and the tier still up. The third runs a store of 12 slots at 0.1 s a
write past its bound of 0.54 s, which is reported complete and failed
with no fault, while the store queued behind it lands. The fourth checks
that an overrun store on one of three ranks publishes nothing, releases
its GPU references, and keeps the tier up. The start-line test now
checks the rank. The CUDA path of an overrun was not tested, and no
load overran during the hardware run.

Upstream status: the patch is proposed to spark-ds41f in
experiments/2026-11-22-kv-disk-tier and has not been submitted to
local-inference-lab/vllm.
